✅ Positive Test Cases for Withdraw Functionality
Verify user successfully clicks on the "Withdraw" button from the Home page and is redirected to the withdraw page.
Verify that the user can successfully withdraw the minimum allowed amount (e.g., ₹50).
Verify that the user can successfully withdraw the maximum allowed amount (e.g., ₹6000).
Verify that the user’s available balance is updated automatically after a successful withdrawal.
Verify that the "Proceed" button is enabled when a valid withdrawal amount is entered.
Verify that the user can withdraw an amount equal to their current available balance.
Verify that the user can successfully click on the +₹1000, +₹2500, +₹5000 buttons to update the amount field and proceed.
Verify that the user can withdraw by selecting different payment methods like "Normal" and "Express" options.
Verify that when the user enters a valid withdrawal amount (e.g., ₹2500), they are able to successfully proceed and withdraw the money.
Verify that the user is able to enter the amount and proceed by selecting the "Normal" withdrawal option.
Verify that the user is able to select "Express" withdrawal option and proceeds with the transaction.
Verify that after selecting the amount and pressing "Proceed," the user is directed to the correct payment gateway page for further steps.
Verify that the user receives a confirmation message after a successful withdrawal.
Verify that the withdrawal history is updated after a successful withdrawal.
Verify that the withdrawal amount is correctly deducted from the user’s balance after the transaction is complete.
Verify that the withdrawal request is processed successfully within the expected time frame (e.g., within 2 minutes for normal, within 30 seconds for express).
Verify that the user can successfully withdraw using the "Bank Transfer" payment method.
Verify that the user can successfully withdraw using the "PayTM" payment method.
Verify that the user can successfully withdraw using the "UPI" payment method.
Verify that the user can withdraw after entering all required details (bank account number, IFSC, etc.) correctly.
Verify that the withdrawal confirmation page displays correct details (e.g., amount, payment method, transaction reference).
Verify that the user can successfully withdraw after entering valid UTR (transaction ID).
Verify that the withdrawal process completes successfully when there is a stable internet connection.
Verify that the user can see the updated balance on the withdraw page after submitting a withdrawal request.
Verify that the user can withdraw successfully if the payment gateway and bank account are verified.
Verify that all mandatory fields (bank account details, amount, UTR) are validated correctly before proceeding with the withdrawal.
Verify that after entering an amount (e.g., ₹1000) and clicking on the "Proceed" button, the withdrawal request is successfully processed.
Verify that withdrawal request is processed successfully and the balance is updated after entering the correct amount in the withdrawal field.
Verify that the user can withdraw without any errors when the withdrawal method is correctly chosen.
Verify that the "Proceed" button is disabled when the amount is invalid or below the minimum required withdrawal amount (e.g., ₹49).


❌ Negative Test Cases for Withdraw Functionality
Verify user clicks on "Withdraw" button without being logged in — user should be redirected to login page.
Verify redirection fails if the withdraw page URL is broken or incorrectly configured.
Verify when user tries to withdraw an amount greater than the available balance — should show an error.
Verify "Proceed" button is disabled when the withdraw amount field is left blank.
Verify "Proceed" button remains disabled when entered amount is below the minimum allowed (e.g., ₹49).
Verify user enters non-numeric input (e.g., "abc") in the amount field — should show validation error.
Verify user enters special characters (e.g., @$#%) in the amount field — should show validation error.
Verify user enters negative amount (e.g., -₹100) in the amount field — should not proceed.
Verify user enters amount exceeding the maximum limit (e.g., ₹6001 if ₹6000 is max) — should show error.
Verify user enters decimal values beyond allowed precision (e.g., ₹50.999) — should not accept.
Verify withdrawing amount without entering required bank account details — should block withdrawal.
Verify withdrawing to an unverified or inactive payment method — should show warning or error.
Verify that auto-refresh fails when balance is updated but Internet is disconnected.
Verify user tries to withdraw amount and clicks "Back" during transaction — should prompt or prevent loss of data.
Verify withdrawal fails gracefully if server is down at the time of submission.
Verify user initiates rapid repeated withdrawals — system should throttle or block spam attempts.
Verify user clicks on "Proceed" without network connection — proper error message should be shown.
Verify withdrawing amount with leading zeros (e.g., 000050) — should be parsed and validated correctly.
Verify empty amount field and selecting withdrawal method — should not proceed.
Verify selecting invalid withdrawal method or corrupted option — system should show fallback or error.
Verify user tries to access withdrawal page via direct URL manipulation with invalid parameters.
Verify incorrect data or missing logs after withdrawal — system should handle it without crashing.
Verify large withdrawal (within allowed limit) during peak hours — ensure no timeout or failure due to load.
Verify network disconnect during the withdrawal process after amount is deducted — must reconcile or retry.
Verify decimal values near boundary values (e.g., ₹49.99, ₹6000.01) — must validate properly.

For Admin

✅ Positive Test Cases for Withdraw Tab – Admin Side
Verify redirection to the Withdraw page when the user clicks on the "Withdraw" tab from the navigation bar.
Verify that the Withdraw details on the Withdraw page match the client-side data.
Verify that the Status of each withdrawal request is displayed correctly and matches client-side information.
Verify that User Details (e.g., name, user ID, email) in the Withdraw page match with the client-side records.
Verify that the Withdrawal Amount shown in the page matches the client's request.
Verify that the Risk (%) value is accurately displayed and calculated as per backend logic.
Verify that Approval Details (approver name, date/time) are correctly shown and synced with the client side.
Verify that the Withdraw Reference (transaction ID or internal reference) is accurate and matches client logs.
Verify that Remaining or Turn Around Time (TAT) is calculated and displayed correctly for pending withdrawals.
Verify that Gateway Details (mode of withdrawal such as Paytm, UPI, Bank Transfer) are shown correctly.
Verify that additional Info (remarks, status updates) is displayed in the Withdraw page accurately.
Verify that "View Bank Details" expands to show the correct linked bank account for the user.
Verify that Logs section records every change or action taken (status change, comments, etc.).
Verify that the Action buttons (Approve, Reject) are displayed and functional for eligible withdrawals.
Verify that clicking "Approve" successfully marks the withdrawal as approved and updates the status/logs.
Verify that clicking "Reject" marks the withdrawal as rejected and allows entering a rejection reason.
Verify that withdrawals below a certain amount (e.g., Rs. 200 or Rs. 300) are auto-approved as per system rules.
Verify that withdrawals below a threshold are auto-rejected based on risk analysis or pre-set rules.
Verify that the system shows appropriate error messages or offline indicators when no Internet connection is available.
Verify that clicking the "Export" button successfully downloads the admin data in a proper file format (CSV/XLS).
Verify that clicking the "Export" button when no data is available shows a “No data to export” or similar prompt.
Verify that the total withdrawal amount is calculated and displayed correctly on the Withdraw page (e.g., Total: ₹X).

❌ Negative Test Cases for Withdraw Tab – Admin
Verify behavior when user clicks on the "Withdraw" tab with no internet connection.
Verify if withdraw details show mismatched data compared to client side (e.g., incorrect amount or user info).
Verify system behavior when Status field is blank or shows an undefined status.
Verify when User Details are missing or partially loaded (e.g., only user ID but no name or email).
Verify when the Amount field is null or shows incorrect format (e.g., “abc” or “-100”).
Verify if Risk (%) field shows a negative or value above 100.
Verify when Approval Details are missing (no approver name or timestamp).
Verify Withdraw Reference field with duplicate or blank values.
Verify when Remaining/Turn Around Time is showing as a negative value.
Verify if Gateway Details are missing or show an unsupported payment mode.
Verify View Bank Details expands to show empty or incorrect data.
Verify Logs section fails to show any previous activity on withdrawal.
Verify clicking “Approve” without a valid withdrawal reference.
Verify clicking “Reject” without providing a rejection reason (if mandatory).
Verify auto-approval happens incorrectly for an amount above configured threshold.
Verify auto-rejection fails to trigger on blacklisted user or high-risk percentage.
Verify Export button when clicked repeatedly within seconds.
Verify Export button click when no withdrawal data exists.
Verify Exported file contains mismatched or partial data compared to displayed table.
Verify “Total Withdrawal Amount” field displays incorrect total due to rounding or sync issue.
